WEBVTT

NOTE
Cue boundaries are taken from the narration's own measured pauses
(ffmpeg silencedetect, -35 dB / 0.28 s), not estimated from word counts, so the
captions land on the speech rather than near it. The text is the script exactly
as spoken; the same words appear on the page as a transcript.

1
00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:02.140
Hello. I'm Vikram Deshpande.

2
00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.280
What you're watching is an AI-generated avatar —

3
00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.000
my photograph, my own cloned voice,

4
00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:09.180
rendered by a model.

5
00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.230
I'm telling you that straight away,

6
00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.370
because I build systems that are not allowed
to fabricate their own evidence.

7
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.350
Everything else here is real.

8
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.660
The figures come from my CV, and from
repositories you can open and read.

9
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.270
Where something could not honestly be measured,
the page says so.

10
00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:29.150
If any of it is useful to you,
I would welcome a conversation.
